    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0178" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg98"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Belgian Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-10-06"><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>By telegram dated October 6, the Belgian Government instructs the legation of
                    Belgium at Washington to ask the Government of the United States to authorize
                    the American cruiser at Cape Haitien to concert with the consul of Belgium for
                    the protection of common interests in the Bayeux plantation.</p>
            </div>
